-- Found by experiments_nest lm-product-of-experts-decoding (2026-10-14),
-- task batched-mask-variant-neural-read-nests-v-deep. The agreement
-- product spelled with a Bool flag, (a, a == b), over a contiguous 250-value
-- neural domain. The batched per-mask variant for a query whose second slot
-- is ANY (Main__m01) reads P(a = sample[0]) as a 250-deep right-nested `+`
-- chain of where_anchored(k == sample[0], raw[..., k], 0.0), past CPython's
-- 200-parenthesis limit; the module did not import until the batched backend
-- spilled deep lines (task batched-enum-comprehension-exceeds-parser-nesting).
-- Both experts uniform here. no-normalization: sampling cannot cover the
-- 250 x 2 support (and took two minutes trying).
-- The (_, ANY) variant now reads the network with one range-guarded
-- nn_gather instead (IRGatherPass); the 249/250/-1 rows pin the range
-- edges, where a clamped gather without the guard would read slot 0/249.
no-normalization
